"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false,"staleReadFileStateHint":"[This command modified 1 file you've previously read: PLAN.md. Call Read before editing.]","bashEditDiff":{"files":[{"filePath":"/Users/tacoda/tacoda/bastion/DECISIONS.md","hunks":[{"oldStart":85,"oldLines":6,"newStart":85,"newLines":7,"lines":[" | D56 | A constraint or capability is feedforward, which guides the agent before it acts (a rule it is told, a skill, an agent, a note on what it may do), or feedback, which checks what it did (a word match, a hook, a review check, a reviewer); it comes from the workspace's charter or from Bastion. Told, checked and enforced give way: a feedforward rule is said to the agent, a feedback one always blocks, and a grant keeps ask or allowed. Items are on or off at a step or for every step of a workflow; the level for every workflow stays in the data but out of the app for now. |"," | D57 | Rules live on three pages, Constraints, Capabilities and Permissions, each with a Global view and a Workflows view that picks the workflows and steps an item applies to. A step lists what applies at it, read-only. The charter shows on a Workspaces page; Bastion still applies it, but it is not edited with Bastion's rules. This replaces D53's \"no Constraints or Capabilities page\". |"," | D58 | Nothing is global. Each rule, agent, skill, hook, reviewer and grant applies only where it is selected: one step, a workflow's steps, some workflows, or all workflows. An item with no selection applies nowhere. A charter's items apply to their workspace's jobs, and the app edits them as a commit on a new branch of the workspace's repository, never on its base branch. Every page shows all servers or one; on All servers a row names its server, and a change goes to that server. This replaces D57's Global view with All workflows, and D53's rule that only record pages span servers. |","+| D59 | A field note is what a job taught, one sentence signed by the person who wrote it, about the workspace (the project) or about Bastion (its workflows and harness). It is an audit entry on the job, so the chain signs it and nothing rewrites it. A workspace's notes are its atlas, where the next request starts. A job that comes home, landed or in the marsh, draws its way back to the atlas. |"," "," ## Open questions"," "]}]},{"filePath":"/Users/tacoda/tacoda/bastion/PLAN.md","hunks":[{"oldStart":297,"oldLines":6,"newStart":297,"newLines":22,"lines":[" - A checklist on Jobs until it's done: add a workspace, check a model,","   send a first request."," ","+### X. Exploration: learning, discovery, feedback","+","+The app should feel like an expedition, and improve itself from what jobs","+teach.","+","+- Done: the trail's way home to the atlas, field notes about the","+  workspace or Bastion (D59), and the marsh on every trail.","+- The Map: each harbor town opens its workspace's atlas, with its notes","+  by workspace and by Bastion.","+- A route's wear: the Map shows where recent jobs on each workflow wait,","+  turn back and end in the marsh.","+- A lesson from the atlas: a Bastion note offers \"make this a check\" or","+  \"add this as guidance\", applied at the step it came from.","+- Everything clickable lifts a little on hover, as the landmarks do.","+- A legend on each chart that teaches its marks.","+"," ## Open questions"," "," - **Plugin hooks that need the host.** A Claude Code hook runs on the"]}]}],"moreFiles":0,"changedFiles":["/Users/tacoda/tacoda/bastion/DECISIONS.md","/Users/tacoda/tacoda/bastion/PLAN.md"]}},"serverClassifierContext":{"request":"e10c65c0-0451-493f-bce1-c80c06204619","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/Users/tacoda/tacoda/bastion","root":"/Users/tacoda/tacoda/bastion","branch":"main","default_branch":"main","status":{"clean":false,"counts":{"staged":0,"modified":9,"untracked":null,"untracked_normal":1},"porcelain":null,"truncated":false},"visibility":{"origin":null,"push_remote":"origin","remotes":[],"visibility_cache":[]}},"live_cwd":"/Use