{"parentUuid":"ebc3e9cf-2205-4bb4-a411-ac5d879f8a1c","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgynTf2G2exp2rbCYVccQ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":885,"cache_read_input_tokens":719854,"output_tokens":867,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":117},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":885,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":867,"cache_read_input_tokens":719854,"cache_creation_input_tokens":885,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":885},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"e7da060e-3652-4310-9951-80e3807032a8","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CgynTeYF1Td9QyrW38aNV","attributionMcpServer":"plugin:codescene:codescene","attributionMcpTool":"pre_commit_code_health_safeguard","type":"assistant","uuid":"9bca9750-8bbd-42e9-a1c8-b7d946887548","timestamp":"2026-11-12T21:59:26.082Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"4fe51ecd-d6cc-423f-a39e-68f5e5b7e45e","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/tacoda/tacoda/bastion","sessionId":"4fe51ecd-d6cc-423f-a39e-68f5e5b7e45e","version":"2.1.285","gitBranch":"main","slug":"parsed-tinkering-blum"}
{"parentUuid":"9bca9750-8bbd-42e9-a1c8-b7d946887548","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgynTf2G2exp2rbCYVccQ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The return trail and the atlas work in the app, but the disk is full, so this round is staged and **not committed**.\n\n**What's built (staged):**\n- **The way home.** Once a job lands, fails or stops, a dotted trail runs from the summit, or from the marsh, back to **the atlas**: a domed hall on the coast, under the outpost.\n- **The marsh on every job's trail.** It's drawn faint under the summit. When a job fails or stops, the route turns down into it and it gets a red X.\n- **Field notes (D59).**\n  - Pressing the atlas opens a card in place with the job's notes and a short form: one sentence, about **the workspace** or **Bastion**, then Sign.\n  - On the server, a note is an audit entry on the job, signed by the person who wrote it, so nothing can rewrite it.\n  - New routes: `POST /jobs/{id}/note` (needs the right to act on the job) and `GET /atlas` (every note, newest first, with the job's request, workspace, and whether it landed).\n  - Each workspace's notes form its own atlas.\n- **Live check.** I signed one test note on test job `j1c15ab9b`: \"Test note: the named test made the change easy to check.\" It read back as \"Ian Johnson · about the workspace · just now\". It's permanent in the local audit chain, by design.\n- **Docs.** D59 is in DECISIONS.md. PLAN.md has a new section \"X. Exploration\", with what's done and what's left:\n  - each harbor town on the Map opens its workspace's atlas;\n  - route wear: where recent jobs wait, turn back, or end in the marsh;\n  - \"make this a check\" from a Bastion note;\n  - hover lift on everything clickable;\n  - a legend on each chart.\n\n**Why it's not committed:**\n- The desktop and server tests passed, and the safeguard passes.\n- But after that, the CodeScene safeguard flagged `Trail.draw` as too long, so I moved the way-home drawing into `homeward()`. That edit hasn't been compiled.\n- Workspace clippy then failed with `No space left on device`. Only 118Mi is free.\n\nFree about 5Gi, and I'll run clippy and the tests, commit, push, and continue with the atlas on the Map and the hover lift."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":885,"cache_read_input_tokens":719854,"output_tokens":867,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":117},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":885,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":867,"cache_read_input_tokens":719854,"cache_creation_input_tokens":885,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":885},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"e7da060e-3652-4310-9951-80e3807032a8","apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011CgynTeYF1Td9QyrW38aNV","attributionMcpServer":"plugin:codescene:codescene","attributionMcpTool":"pre_commit_code_health_safeguard","type":"assistant","uuid":"357dd4eb-ad58-4ea5-820b-3318d1e211d3","timestamp":"2026-11-12T21:59:26.181Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"4fe51ecd-d6cc-423f-a39e-68f5e5b7e45e","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/tacoda/tacoda/bastion","sessionId":"4fe51ecd-d6cc-423f-a39e-68f5e5b7e45e","version":"2.1.285","gitBranch":"main","slug":"parsed-tinkering-blum"}
